title: oliverNeutral
---
<<set $JohnPresent to false>>
<<set $DanielPresent to true>>
Daniel: Hm. Perhaps the balance of truth shifts towards you. Oliver?

Oliver: I am here.

Daniel: Very good. We will speak to you soon. 

You look over at Oliver. He lives on the other side of town, so you haven’t seen him in a couple of days. He’s  a couple years older than you.

Would he defend you or would he defend Esther? 

He was too unpredictable.

He was only a couple years older than you. You could trust that he would side with you over an old crone. 

Esther bought bread from him quite often. He would be loyal to his customers. 

If it came down to it…
-> You could bat your eyelashes. Bend him to your will with a blush and a smile. 
-> Plead for his help. Appeal to his need to control, to dominate. There was nothing more invigorating than saving a young, helpless girl. 
-> Stay silent. Sometimes this was the safer choice.
<<set $OliverPresent to false>>
<<jump father>>
