title: Act3_Lizzy
tags: act3 witness_lizzy
---
You take a deep breath and realize that your hands are trembling.  
The same hands that held many of the people in this room when they were babies.  
That wiped the brows of every mother and soothed every father.

You look around you.

You cannot fathom it.  
The gift of giving life was something you had always worshipped.  
A gift from God.  
A beacon of hope in a time where life was—well… a fight for survival.

But now?  
The faces that had once gazed upon you with love and kindness look at you differently.

All around you are expressions of disgust and resentment.  
Parents pull their children close.  
Women shake their heads and pray.  
Fingers point.

You are vilified.

In everyone’s eyes you have sentenced a child to unbelievable pain and suffering.  
There is nothing worse than betraying your people, and thus betraying God.

There is nothing you can do or say that will matter.  
If you plead guilty, you will die.

But no one pleads guilty.

You look at your pale, withered skin.  
Feel the beating of your fragile heart under your breast.  
To lie about who you were…  
to betray the faith that you lived by…

It is inconceivable.

You are not a coward.  
Rebecca Nurse was not a coward.  
Neither was Mary Eastey or John Proctor.

Steady yourself and reply…

-> "I maintain my innocence above all else."
    John: Very well.
    Daniel: Let’s see what they think. Neighbors! Who do you think is guilty? Is it just Esther? Or is there another witch in this room?
    <<if $prudenceFavor >= $estherFavor and $prudenceFavor >= $ruthFavor>>
            The crowd cries out Prudence’s name.
            Daniel: Esther. Prudence. We sentence you both to die.
            <<jump Scene_End>>
    <<elseif $estherFavor > $prudenceFavor and $estherFavor >= $ruthFavor>>
        The crowd cries out your name.
        Daniel: Esther. We sentence you to die.
        <<jump Scene_End>>
     <<elseif $ruthFavor > $prudenceFavor and $ruthFavor > $estherFavor>>
        The crowd cries out Ruth’s name.
        Daniel: Esther. Ruth. We sentence you both to die.
            <<jump Scene_End>>
    <<else>>
        Confusion spreads through the crowd, but their fear quickly turns on you.
        Daniel: Esther. We sentence you to die.
        <<jump Scene_End>>
    <<endif>>
    <<jump Scene_End>>
-> "There is a witch in this room, but it is not me."
    John: Then who do you accuse?

    You look around you and name…
    -> "Laura, my mentee."
        Laura: The witch lies!
        Daniel: Perhaps. But you lent her your ear.  
        You gave her your time.  
        You called her a teacher.
        Daniel: We cannot risk letting you live.
        John: It is the belief of us, who speak for all of you, Salem, that our life is a covenant with God...  
        Sin is a rotting limb. If we do not cut it off, it consumes us entirely.
        Daniel: Laura. Esther. We sentence both of you to die.
        <<jump Scene_End>>
    -> "Ruth, the mother of my accuser."
        Ruth: She… she lies!
        Daniel: Perhaps. But you have proved untrustworthy.  
        You spoke too much, woman.
        Daniel: We cannot risk letting you live.
        John: It is the belief of us, who speak for all of you, Salem, that our life is a covenant with God...  
        Sin is a rotting limb. If we do not cut it off, it consumes us entirely.
        Daniel: Laura. Ruth. We sentence both of you to die.
        <<jump Scene_End>>
    -> "Prudence, the accuser."
        Prudence: Why would the good people of this town believe you over me?

        Daniel: The girl is right. Lizzy affirmed that when she spoke.

        Daniel: Let us see what the people believe.

        <<if $prudenceFavor <= $estherFavor and $prudenceFavor <= $ruthFavor>>
            The crowd cries out Prudence’s name.
            Daniel: Esther. Prudence. We sentence you both to die.
            <<jump Scene_End>>

        <<elseif $estherFavor < $prudenceFavor and $estherFavor <= $ruthFavor>>
            The crowd cries out your name.
            Daniel: Esther. We sentence you to die.
            <<jump Scene_End>>

        <<elseif $ruthFavor < $prudenceFavor and $ruthFavor < $estherFavor>>
            The crowd cries out Ruth’s name.
            Daniel: Esther. Ruth. We sentence you both to die.
            <<jump Scene_End>>
        <<else>>
            Confusion spreads through the crowd, but their fear quickly turns on you.
            Daniel: Esther. We sentence you to die.
            <<jump Scene_End>>
        <<endif>>
===
